          'Instance attributes belong to individual objects, while class attributes are shared through the class unless an instance overrides them.',
          'Use instance attributes for values that vary per object. A mutable class attribute such as a list is shared by every instance and can cause surprising behavior; initialize per-instance collections in __init__.',
          'class Student:\n    school = "North Campus"\n    def __init__(self, name):\n        self.name = name\n\nfirst = Student("Ari")\nsecond = Student("Kai")',
